#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161681 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162115 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a62aa30b-6bf5-5c06-bb1f-8269a6806368" :knowledge-point/title "Maximum Likelihood Estimators for Discrete Probability Distributions"}] :question/id #uuid "ce0d131b-ec10-5895-942f-2bece346c152" :question/math-academy-id "e-10107" :question/problem "Given that the log-likelihood function for a particular sample of independent Bernoulli random variables is\n\n$$\nl(\\theta) = 3\\ln\\theta + 4\\ln(1-\\theta),\n$$\n\nwhat is the maximum likelihood estimate $\\widehat{\\,\\theta\\,}$ from this sample?" :question/worked-solution "In order to find the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta,$ we calculate the derivative of the log-likelihood function, set the derivative equal to zero, and solve for $\\theta.$\n\nFirst, we take the derivative of $l(\\theta){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}l}{\\text{d}\\theta } & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\theta }(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta +4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-\\theta )) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\theta }+\\frac{4}{1-\\theta }\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\theta }+\\frac{4}{\\theta -1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we set the derivative equal to $0$ and solve for $\\theta{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{\\theta }+\\frac{4}{\\theta -1} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{3(\\theta -1)+4\\theta }{\\theta (\\theta -1)} & =0 \\\\ 3(\\theta -1)+4\\theta  & =0 \\\\ 7\\theta -3 & =0 \\\\ 7\\theta  & =3 \\\\ \\theta  & =\\frac{3}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, for this sample, the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta$ is $\\widehat{\\,\\theta\\,} =  \\dfrac{3}{7}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161682 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162116 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "78241be4-1db7-554c-a7ce-7532345f3f5a" :knowledge-point/title "Maximum Likelihood Estimators for Continuous Probability Distributions"}] :question/id #uuid "dd2ad84f-1fa2-5f7c-9af3-db9dce4b5133" :question/math-academy-id "e-10108" :question/problem "Given that the log-likelihood function for a particular sample of independent normal random variables $X_i\\sim N(\\theta,1)$ is\n\n$$\nl(\\theta) = -6\\ln(2\\pi)-8.4 + 12.1\\, \\! \\theta - 6\\ \\! \\theta^2,\n$$\n\nwhat is the maximum likelihood estimate $\\widehat{\\,\\theta\\,}$ for this sample? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "In order to find the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta,$ we calculate the derivative of the log-likelihood function, set the derivative equal to zero, and solve for $\\theta.$\n\nFirst, we take the derivative of $l(\\theta){:}$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}l}{\\text{d}\\theta } & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\theta }(-6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2\\pi )-8.4+12.1\\,\\,\\theta -6\\text{ }\\,{\\theta }^{2}) \\\\  & =12.1-12\\text{ }\\,\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we set the derivative equal to $0$ and solve for $\\theta{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12.1-12\\text{ }\\,\\theta  & =0 \\\\ 12\\text{ }\\,\\theta  & =12.1 \\\\ \\theta  & ≈1.008\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, for this sample, the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta$ is $\\widehat{\\,\\theta\\,} \\approx 1.008,$ rounded to $3$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162395 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162115 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a62aa30b-6bf5-5c06-bb1f-8269a6806368" :knowledge-point/title "Maximum Likelihood Estimators for Discrete Probability Distributions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98fd53c6-1ce1-5e29-9342-f54498e4657c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159573} {:answer/id #uuid "a1b9c065-0650-5950-b74e-3025af0b5186" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159574} {:answer/id #uuid "0b801eae-251d-5746-a091-62c984a643d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 