to $0$ and solve for $\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{\\theta }+\\frac{1}{\\theta -1} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{5(\\theta -1)+\\theta }{\\theta (\\theta -1)} & =0 \\\\ 5(\\theta -1)+\\theta  & =0 \\\\ 6\\theta -5 & =0 \\\\ 6\\theta  & =5 \\\\ \\theta  & =\\frac{5}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, for this sample, the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta $ is $\\overset{^}{\\,\\theta \\,}=\\frac{5}{6}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527160 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162116 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "78241be4-1db7-554c-a7ce-7532345f3f5a" :knowledge-point/title "Maximum Likelihood Estimators for Continuous Probability Distributions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5562092f-3fe0-5bcf-8339-c7daec6026f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.208" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526678} {:answer/id #uuid "56b4bf5e-9806-5a09-a3b3-65589f4e73ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.213" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526679} {:answer/id #uuid "8bedb81d-563d-5133-aea2-1add3162bcde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.276" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526783} {:answer/id #uuid "aa8e2520-683e-5f18-9745-b1b59e87e0a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.412" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526831} {:answer/id #uuid "cf461d27-016b-5aa4-a77d-15596b89f756" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.316" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526899}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cf461d27-016b-5aa4-a77d-15596b89f756" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.316" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526899} :answer-field/id #uuid "34a1e506-0c01-548c-8aeb-dbb4e0856d79" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527033}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4510ff72-383e-5b2d-aa54-f6d78aa69e2d" :question/math-academy-id "q-159939" :question/problem "Given that the log-likelihood function for a particular sample of independent exponential random variables is\n\n$$\nl(\\theta )=5\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta -15.8\\text{ }\\,\\theta ,\n$$\n\nwhat is the maximum likelihood estimate $\\overset{^}{\\,\\theta \\,}$ from this sample? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "In order to find the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta ,$ we calculate the derivative of the log-likelihood function, set the derivative equal to zero, and solve for $\\theta .$\n\nFirst, we take the derivative of $l(\\theta ):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}l}{\\text{d}\\theta } & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\theta }(5\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta -15.8\\text{ }\\,\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\theta }-15.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we set the derivative equal to $0$ and solve for $\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{\\theta }-15.8 & =0 \\\\ \\frac{5}{\\theta } & =15.8 \\\\ 5 & =15.8\\text{ }\\,\\theta  \\\\ \\theta  & ≈0.316\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, for this sample, the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta $ is $\\overset{^}{\\,\\theta \\,}≈0.316,$ rounded to $3$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527212 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162116 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "78241be4-1db7-554c-a7ce-7532345f3f5a" :knowledge-point/title "Maximum Likelihood Estimators for Continuous Probability Distributions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01b7e61a-87f8-5dfb-b095-ddd7b27158f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.765" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526503} {:answer/id #uuid "3de46f7c-9501-5c63-9068-1ec131a5e103" :a