er/value "0.788" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526743} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e02fd70-4bfa-5ee0-87ea-68ee321a3054" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527017}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "54d12174-c052-5371-9f75-2200e071a1fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-159945" :question/problem "Given that the log-likelihood function for a particular sample of independent normal random variables is\n\n$$\nl(\\theta )=-8\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2\\pi )-9.6+12.6\\text{ }\\,\\theta -8\\text{ }\\,{\\theta }^{2},\n$$\n\nwhat is the maximum likelihood estimate $\\overset{^}{\\,\\theta \\,}$ from this sample? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "In order to find the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta ,$ we calculate the derivative of the log-likelihood function, set the derivative equal to zero, and solve for $\\theta .$\n\nFirst, we take the derivative of $l(\\theta ):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}l}{\\text{d}\\theta } & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\theta }(-8\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2\\pi )-9.6+12.6\\text{ }\\,\\theta -8\\text{ }\\,{\\theta }^{2}) \\\\  & =12.6-16\\text{ }\\,\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we set the derivative equal to $0$ and solve for $\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12.6-16\\text{ }\\,\\theta  & =0 \\\\ 16\\text{ }\\,\\theta  & =12.6 \\\\ \\theta  & ≈0.788\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, for this sample, the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta $ is $\\overset{^}{\\,\\theta \\,}≈0.788,$ rounded to $3$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527180 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162115 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a62aa30b-6bf5-5c06-bb1f-8269a6806368" :knowledge-point/title "Maximum Likelihood Estimators for Discrete Probability Distributions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4162e3d9-b07a-5986-95b7-183bc014b786" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526630} {:answer/id #uuid "694a6d77-b1f1-591c-bc99-15a19344806a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526714} {:answer/id #uuid "d2d0294e-3e9f-5fe9-9082-3c690994a0b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526909} {:answer/id #uuid "ea506d61-f445-598b-b7b4-71d4e5999d00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526969} {:answer/id #uuid "f262d641-ad09-5541-a1b9-b14c2d786ffa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526980}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "694a6d77-b1f1-591c-bc99-15a19344806a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526714} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f74069f-b86f-503f-a061-d9ec00b1c8bf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527027}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8cb508aa-a9ee-56b2-be2a-f7d71a96d61c" :question/math-academy-id "q-159963" :question/problem "Given that the log-likelihood function for a particular sample of independent Bernoulli random variables is\n\n$$\nl(\\theta )=8\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta +12\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-\\theta ),\n$$\n\nwhat is the maximum likelihood estimate $\\overset{^}{\\,\\theta \\,}$ from this sample?" :question/worked-solution "In order to find the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta ,$ we calculate the derivative of the log-likelihood function, set the derivative equal to zero, and solve for $\\theta .$\n\nFirst, we take the derivative of $l(\\theta ):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}l}{\\text{d}\\theta } & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\theta }(8\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta +12\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-\\theta )) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\theta }+\\frac{12}{1-\\theta }\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\theta }+\\frac{12}{\\theta -1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we set the derivative equal to $0$ and solve for $\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8}{\\theta }+\\frac{12}{\\theta -1} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{8(\\theta -1)+12\\theta }{\\theta (\\theta -1)} & =0 \\\\ 8(\\theta -1)+12\\theta  & =0 \\\\ 20\\theta -8 & =0 \\\\ 20\\theta  & =8 \\\\ \\theta  & =\\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, for this sample, the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta $ is $\\overset{^}{\\,\\theta \\,}=\\frac{2}{5}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527200 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162115 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a62aa30b-6bf5-5c06-bb1f-8269a6806368" :knowledge-point/title "Maximum Likelihood Estimators for Discrete Probability Distributions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0450f0af-5d9b-567c-a1ad-d112306dcc16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526511} {:answer/id #uuid "92c2529a-c481-5299-855e-40b34693e071" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526790} {:answer/id #uuid "9b090b25-4146-55a8-a5b6-04376c6065c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526804} {:answer/id #uuid "c44e79cb-7368-5b47-96a3-d466cfa63dcf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526877} {:answer/id #uuid "fd968792-04b8-50fc-80